🧠 First, the simple definitions

Coupling = How much two modules/classes depend on each other.
Cohesion = How focused a single module/class is on doing ONE job well.

The golden rule: 👉 Low Coupling + High Cohesion = 🔥 Good Code

💔 Coupling — Think of it like a relationship

Imagine two friends, Raj and Priya.

High Coupling (Bad) 😬
Raj literally can't do ANYTHING without calling Priya first. Wanna order food? Ask Priya. Wanna pick a movie? Ask Priya. If Priya's phone dies, Raj's whole life stops.

That's tightly coupled code — if you change one class, you're forced to change five others too. One small edit = everything breaks. 😵

Low Coupling (Good) ✅
Raj and Priya are independent people who occasionally team up but can function fine on their own. If Priya's busy, Raj still lives his life.

That's loosely coupled code — modules interact through clean interfaces, but don't need to know each other's internal business.

java
// ❌ Tightly coupled
class Car {
    Engine engine = new PetrolEngine(); // stuck with this forever
}

// ✅ Loosely coupled
class Car {
    Engine engine; // any engine type can be plugged in
    Car(Engine engine) { this.engine = engine; }
}
🎯 Cohesion — Think of it like a job role

Low Cohesion (Bad) 😩
Imagine hiring a "chef" who also has to do accounting, clean toilets, and fix the wifi. He's overloaded, confused, and bad at everything because his job isn't focused.

java
class Utility {
    void cookFood() {}
    void calculateTax() {}
    void sendEmail() {}
    void fixWifi() {}
} 
// bro this class has an identity crisis 💀

High Cohesion (Good) ✅
A chef who ONLY cooks. That's it. That's his job. He's a master at it because he's laser-focused.

java
class Chef {
    void cookFood() {}
    void chopVegetables() {}
    void plateDish() {}
}
// clean, focused, does ONE thing really well 👨‍🍳
📊 Quick Cheat Table
	Loose Coupling ✅	High Cohesion ✅
Meaning	Modules don't depend heavily on each other	Each module does ONE clear job
Goal	Easy to change one thing without breaking others	Easy to understand & maintain
Bad version	Tight coupling (everything connected, fragile)	Low cohesion (messy, does everything)
🥡 One-line takeaway to remember forever:

"Talk less to others (low coupling), focus more on your own job (high cohesion)."